  (text "BRIDGEVILLE RTK BASE - DRV8871 RELAY DRIVER (STAGE 1)\nESP32 control and Adafruit DRV8871 breakout wiring only"
    (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 1034f80b-b80b-4820-aa3b-1e373a93a201)
  )
  (text "DIRECT WIRING\n1. ESP32 GPIO25 -> DRV8871 IN1\n2. ESP32 GPIO26 -> DRV8871 IN2\n3. Fused battery +12V -> breakout POWER + terminal\n4. Battery negative -> breakout POWER - terminal\n5. ESP32 GND -> same battery negative/common ground\n6. Breakout MOTOR outputs -> the two coil wires of a verified\n   12V single-coil polarity-latching relay"
    (at 25.4 190.5 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 23e4a8ae-c6e6-4a8f-b84a-2fe3e9a3a202)
  )
  (text "DRV8871 CONTROL TABLE\nGPIO25 / IN1   GPIO26 / IN2   RESULT\nLOW            LOW            Outputs high-Z; sleep after about 1 ms\nHIGH           LOW            OUT1 positive relative to OUT2 (pulse SET*)\nLOW            HIGH           OUT2 positive relative to OUT1 (pulse RESET*)\nHIGH           HIGH           Brake; do not use as idle\n\n*SET/RESET polarity depends on the selected relay and coil orientation.\nConfirm with the relay datasheet before final wiring. Use timed pulses only."
    (at 129.54 147.32 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid e5cb7d6f-3661-44c6-98d9-bf80d001a203)
  )
  (text "IMPORTANT PART CHECK\nSRD-12VDC-SL-C is documented by Songle as a conventional monostable SPDT relay,\nnot a single-coil polarity-latching relay. Do not purchase or wire that part for this\nH-bridge pulse-and-hold-power-off design. Select the exact latching relay first; then\nadd its contact pins and physical footprint to the next schematic revision."
    (at 129.54 190.5 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 17194130-1cc4-40ab-9842-e983d190a204)
  )
  (text "Use the breakout's POWER screw terminal for the external 12V supply.\nDo not connect the 12V VM rail to an ESP32 power pin. The breakout accepts\n3.3V GPIO logic and contains 100k input pulldowns in the DRV8871.\nNo flyback diode is placed across a polarity-reversing latching coil."
    (at 25.4 220.98 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 1b3fa44c-69b6-45d0-90fd-28a9e24da205)
  )

